Messages.Body:
@Ankha: Rule 1.6.1.4 talks about what you can or cannot target. It implies that you cannot target the ash heap (since the ash heap is now considered uncontrolled), and it explicitly says you cannot target the uncontrolled region.

I argue that the crypt card is targeted when IotK is played, as part of the announcement of the card. That targeting should then follow the card wherever it goes. It specifically refers to the card as a "card" and not a "vampire" or "minion", meaning that its "state" is not relevant. IotK starts out by targeting a card that is already not in play. And how can IotK continue to target things after it is in the ash heap?

@Maddog: I'm not advocating that more effects should remove cards from the game. What I'm saying is that IotK should always remove a card from the game because that is what it's card text says.
